{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MC-009","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"title","page":1,"quote":"SHAFT"}],"comment":"The drawing title identifies the part as a shaft, but no centre holes are specified for turning between centres. Without centre holes the machinist has no defined datum for lathe work, risking poor concentricity of the turned diameters. The designer should add centre hole callouts (e.g., per ISO 6411) at both ends of the shaft."

    ,
    "recommended_correction": "Add centre hole specifications to both ends of the shaft on page 1."}]}
